WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.835
-My next guest is an
Emmy-winning director, writer,

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.938
and producer who has made films
like "Selma," "13th,"

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.440
and "A Wrinkle in Time."

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.242
The fifth season
of her show "Queen Sugar"

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:12.611
airs Tuesdays
at 8:00 p.m. on OWN.

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:15.014
Here is Ava DuVernay.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.549
-Oh, my good--
-Hey, Jimmy!

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.750
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.085
Thanks for doing the show.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.321
It is so nice
to finally meet you.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.389
-I love you.

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.657
And I watch you every night.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.759
You really helped me
get through quarantine,

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.094
and I just want
to say thank you.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.462
And I just want -- One day,

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.097
I want you to call me
"buddy" or "pal."

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.966
That's all I want.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.500
-Wow, you really do
watch the show.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.802
-So I can feel it,
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:39.272
-You are the best.
I love that you know that.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:42.174
You are honestly --
Not only do I love your work,

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:45.244
but I love your work ethic,
and I love how much you do.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.014
And you go, "Yeah, check this
out. I'm going to write this."

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.415
And then you write it.
Then you produce it.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.017
Then you direct -- I'm like,

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.885
you are one of the busiest
people in the business,

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.387
and it's quality stuff.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.955
There's something
I want to ask you about.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.791
Your company, ARRAY,
launched last week.

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.559
It is called ARRAY Crew,

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:04.731
A-R-R-A-Y Crew, C-R-E-W,
dot com.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.535
Can you explain what this is,
and how can people get involved?

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.802
-Yeah, ARRAY is a collective

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.037
that I founded
about 10 years ago,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.338
and we do all kinds of things.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.574
We distribute films for women
and people of color

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.275
who otherwise wouldn't have
their films distributed.

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.111
We make TV shows and film,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.480
the "When They See Us" and
the "Queen Sugars" of the world.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.851
But we also know that
from being on all these sets,

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.719
you know, when we make
film and television

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.521
that most of the people
behind the scenes

00:01:29.521 --> 00:01:30.789
kind of all look one way.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:33.025
They look like you
more than they look like me.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.460
And so what we want
to try to say

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.963
is both of us should
have a place on set.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.965
And we want to open it up
and make sure

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.699
that people who are
hiring crews --

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:42.635
producers, studios, networks --

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:47.306
know about people of different
cultures, colors,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:51.343
different identities,
ages, physical abilities.

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:54.747
The people who usually we don't
see, we want them to be seen,

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.315
and so that's
what ARRAY Crew is.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.984
-That's wild,
and it's taking off.

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:00.419
-It's really taking off.

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:03.790
The big thing is, we knew
there were crew members there

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.458
who would want to be in
the platform, in the database.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:08.194
But the question is,
could we get the studios

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.895
and the networks
to get behind it?

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.197
And when we launched last week,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.533
every single major studio
and network,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.836
every single one, every
streamer, committed to use it.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.571
And they're using it,
and people are getting jobs

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.940
and getting connected.
And that's all we wanted.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.942
We're a non-profit,
so we just wanted people --

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.243
-That's the key.
-It's free, you know?

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:25.979
It's just connection.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.147
-Great. I love
that you did that. Good for you.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:30.449
I want to talk about
"Queen Sugar."

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:33.486
This is a show you created
and you produced.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.488
And the fifth season
just premiered,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.390
and it's already been renewed
for a sixth.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:40.359
It's very up-to-date, very 2020,
very present.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.161
You ended up rewriting
the whole thing.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.096
Tell everyone what's going on.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:47.066
-Well, you know, this was
the first series I ever did.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:50.803
You know, I was making movies,
so I was used to kind of make
the movie, and it's over.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.006
And this is like,
make a movie every week,

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.341
oh, and you're renewed
for six years!

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.476
Like, we're still
telling the story.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.745
But one of the things about it

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:01.881
is that it's about
a contemporary Black family.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.751
We always took pride in the fact
that we were telling the story

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.752
of Black people
in the here and now.

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.153
And so when
the here and now changed

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.889
and it was COVID,
and it was, you know, politics,

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:13.626
and it was, you know,
a real racial reckoning

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.029
that seemed to be happening
in some corners,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.363
we wanted to deal with that.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.865
And so we changed the story
that we had written

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:20.967
so we could stay true

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.101
to contemporary stories
of Black folk,

00:03:23.101 --> 00:03:24.403
and we rewrote the season

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:27.540
that's basically a flashback
to everything in 2020.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.311
So just, you know, we opened
with, it's the month before.

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.913
It's like February 2020,

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.682
when no one was really
tuned in on the fact

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.851
that this was going to be
something that affected us,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.320
not just people
in other countries.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.887
Then we get to March,
and it's like "Oh, yeah,

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:43.356
I heard something's
happening in Seattle

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.291
with old people
in a old folks home.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.592
Not to do with me."

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:49.729
And then each episode,
it starts to really happen

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.130
in the way that it happened
for most of us

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.899
where it starts
to confront you head-on.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:57.102
-Yeah. The show
is on the OWN network,

00:03:57.102 --> 00:03:59.204
which is Oprah Winfrey's
Network.

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:03.242
All the Oprah wisdom and advice

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:05.044
that she's given over the years,
that I've taken --

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.412
I mean, I do dream journals.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.647
Everyone -- Please,
she's touched everybody.

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:12.217
Is there anything specific
that's always stuck with you?

00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:15.854
-The idea of
nothing bad is happening to you,

00:04:15.854 --> 00:04:17.924
it's happening for you.
-Wow.

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.425
-That was really
a big one for me.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.860
-Is there anything
that Oprah would say

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.762
that you've taught her?

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.730
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:28.667
I think I've taught her
how to put GIFs on her IG.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.769
I've taught her...
-No! Did you teach her --

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:32.705
[ Laughs ]
You upped her GIF game?

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:36.509
-...how to do a Boomerang. Okay,
these are important things,

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:38.344
just like it's not happening
to you, it's happening for you.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.513
-I wish you could teach me
how to do a Boomerang.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.014
I want to show everyone a clip

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:44.583
from next week's episode
of "Queen Sugar."

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.985
Take a look at this.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.387
-What about getting
your crop loan?

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.555
Couldn't that help?

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.992
-Banks ain't given loans
to no farms right now.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.495
To be honest, I'm happy
we ain't harvest.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.828
It would have went to waste

00:04:56.828 --> 00:05:00.500
like all them other farms
throwing out all they product.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.533
[ Sighs ]

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:03.536
Next year,

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:06.272
the soil will be
three times as rich.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.307
We could recoup everything
we didn't make this year,

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:10.943
so I'm -- I'm not
worried about that.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.813
Feel like the land's
gon' take care of us.

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:17.316
Just got to be patient.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.285
-You have a really
beautiful outlook on this.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.587
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.422
I mean, it ain't come easy.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:26.291
We've seen
the ups and downs, but,

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.161
hell, this is where we at.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:31.564
Guess it is what it is, right?

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.765
-Ava DuVernay!

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.801
Season 5 of "Queen Sugar"
airs Tuesday nights

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.537
at 8:00 p.m. on OWN.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.505
Thank you so much again
for coming on the show.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.673
I'm a big fan. Please come back.
Bye, buddy.

00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:42.742
-Thanks, buddy.

